edium", "notes": ["Incumbent Rich McCormick (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Rep. Rich McCormick seeks reelection in a north-metro Atlanta district that leans about eleven points Republican. He has out-raised Democrat Tony Kozycki roughly two-to-one and holds a strong cash advantage. Every major race rating, from Cook to Sabato to the Economist, places the seat in the Safe or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give McCormick about a 94% chance of winning.\n\nKozycki has run an active campaign, securing an endorsement from Senator Jon Ossoff, debating McCormick repeatedly, and benefiting from a Democratic-leaning poll in early October that showed the race within two points. That survey is the only public polling and comes from a partisan sponsor, so it has not moved the overall picture. The district's underlying lean and McCormick's incumbency and resources make him the clear favorite, though the polling hint of competitiveness is the main reason uncertainty remains elevated.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0501, "margin": -12.18}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1218, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0801, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0796, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0786, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0751, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0581, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0723, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0639, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0756, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1071, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1041, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0789, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.027, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0454, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0486, "margi